From 4c3c4b3bf7582dba635ac0f6e95e22b69f31f76a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZHANG Yuntian <yt@radxa.com>
Date: Fri, 8 May 2026 09:22:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 180/268] HACK: drm/tiny: workaround KDE Plasma refresh rate
 issue

DRM_SIMPLE_MODE will be reported as having refresh rate of 0.01Hz in KDE Plasma, causing screen refreshing extremely slowly.

This issue was not observed on GDM login screen.

Currently hardcoding a 1Hz refresh rate for all tinydrm simple modes. Higher refresh rate has been observed to cause touching to be unresponsive, as display consumes too much bus time.

Signed-off-by: ZHANG Yuntian <yt@radxa.com>
